'''Wendell Cason''' (born January 22, 1963) is an American former professional [[American football|football]] player who was a [[cornerback]] and [[Safety (American football position)|safety]] in the [[National Football League]] (NFL).<ref>{{cite news |last=Sheeley |first=Glenn |date=September 18, 1985 |title=Falcons hope for Pleasant surprise from rookie DBs |url=https://www.newspapers.com/article/the-atlanta-journal-falcons-hope-for-ple/181275572/ |work=[[The Atlanta Journal]] |access-date=September 17, 2025}}</ref> He played [[college football]] for the [[Oregon Ducks football|Oregon Ducks]] and was signed by the [[Atlanta Falcons]] as an [[undrafted free agent]] in 1985.
